  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Social and educational reinsertion of separated children in Goma and the Masisi Territory</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will contribute to improving the living conditions of children in Masisi, Democratic Republic of Congo.

The objective of the project, is that using socio-economic reintegration, children and youth affected by armed conflict or from broken families will benefit from the support. For this third year, the aim is to guarantee the education and social reinsertion of children through formal and vocational education. 

Through this project, CAJED and APROFIME in Goma and Masisi, will meet, listen, identify and organise a Participatory Action Research (children&apos;s participation in choosing their reintegration project) with targeted people and communities prior to their formal or vocational education.</narrative>
  </description>
